  "final_answer": "Done. The INT-09 backlog is cleared and all four deliverables are in `/app` (confirmed present and internally consistent):\n\n- **`composite_request_audit.csv`** \u2014 28 audited requests (the 4 withdrawn \u2014 REQ-13/16/26/31 \u2014 excluded per \u00a71), columns `request_id,finding`; clean rows read `none`, breaches joined with `|`.\n- **`account_summary.csv`** \u2014 8 accounts, columns `account_id,account_type,request_count,flagged_requests,escalation`.\n- **`results.json`** \u2014 the eleven \u00a79 figures, each a single number.\n- **`composite_request_memo.md`** \u2014 stand-alone memo for rights review.\n\n**Headline numbers:** 28 audited requests / 8 accounts; 14 flagged, 14 clean; 23 findings raised (6 character, 5 background, 3 consent, 6 commercial, 3 disclosure); 4 accounts escalated (ACC-02, ACC-03, ACC-07, ACC-08) against a 50% batch-wide flagged share.\n\n**The two points to expect questions on at review:**\n- **Supersessions narrow, not widen.** LIC-109 governs LIC-103 and drops the character cap 35%\u219220% (bites REQ-05); LIC-110 governs LIC-105 and narrows background scope `all`\u2192`print_for_sale` only (bites REQ-28's personal_only use).\n- **Lapsed agreements cover nothing.** ACC-08's recorded coverage names print_for_sale \u2014 which would have cleared REQ-30 \u2014 but the lapsed status routes it to `COMMERCIAL_DISTRIBUTION_FLAG` (same for ACC-04 / REQ-14).\n\nThe memo also calls out the false positives INT-09 averts (personal-use allowance clears REQ-01/22/32's character use regardless of cap; the exactly-on-cap REQ-06 is within; LIC-102 and the REQ-11/REQ-28 consents are current though they end on the audit date), names the deciding record for every flagged request, and gives each \u00a78 decision with its measure and limb.",
